<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="description" content="Node.js and Express fundamentals implemented in this course project." />
    <title>{{title}} | Node Course</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/css/main.css" />
    <script src="/assets/js/main.js" defer></script>
  </head>
  <body id="top">
    <div class="page-shell">
      {{> header}}

      <main>
        <section class="page-hero">
          <p class="eyebrow"><span></span> Module 01 / Fundamentals</p>
          <h1>How this server <em>works.</em></h1>
          <p>Four core ideas power the project, from starting Node to rendering a reusable page.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="concept-grid" aria-label="Course concepts">
          <article class="concept-card concept-wide">
            <div class="concept-number">01</div>
            <div>
              <p class="kicker">Runtime</p>
              <h2>Node.js</h2>
              <p>Node runs JavaScript outside the browser. The entry file reads the environment, creates the application and keeps the HTTP server listening for requests.</p>
              <pre><code>const port = process.env.PORT;

app.listen(port, () =&gt; {
  console.log(`Server on ${port}`);
});</code></pre>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article class="concept-card">
            <div class="concept-number">02</div>
            <p class="kicker">Framework</p>
            <h2>Express</h2>
            <p>Routes connect HTTP methods and paths to focused handler functions.</p>
            <pre><code>app.get("/generic", (_req, res) =&gt; {
  res.render("generic");
});</code></pre>
          </article>

          <article class="concept-card accent-card">
            <div class="concept-number">03</div>
            <p class="kicker">Templates</p>
            <h2>Handlebars</h2>
            <p>Views combine HTML with server data. Partials keep navigation and footer markup in one place.</p>
            <div class="mini-code"><span>&#123;&#123;&gt; header&#125;&#125;</span><span>&#123;&#123;title&#125;&#125;</span></div>
          </article>

          <article class="concept-card concept-wide dark-card">
            <div class="concept-number">04</div>
            <div>
              <p class="kicker">Middleware</p>
              <h2>Static assets &amp; 404s</h2>
              <p>Express serves CSS and JavaScript from <code>public</code>. If no route matches, the final wildcard renders a custom response with the correct status.</p>
              <pre><code>app.use(express.static("public"));

app.get("/{*splat}", (req, res) =&gt; {
  res.status(404).render("404");
});</code></pre>
            </div>
          </article>
        </section>

        <section class="section mvc-section" aria-labelledby="mvc-title">
          <div class="section-heading">
            <p class="kicker">Architecture pattern</p>
            <h2 id="mvc-title">Handlebars inside MVC.</h2>
            <p>Handlebars does not implement MVC by itself. In an Express application, it powers the View layer while the server coordinates the other responsibilities.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="mvc-grid">
            <article class="mvc-card">
              <span>M</span>
              <p class="kicker">Model</p>
              <h3>Application data</h3>
              <p>Would contain database access, entities and business rules. This course project has no persistent model yet.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="mvc-card mvc-active">
              <span>V</span>
              <p class="kicker">View</p>
              <h3>Handlebars templates</h3>
              <p>The <code>.hbs</code> files receive data, reuse partials and generate the final HTML sent to the browser.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="mvc-card">
              <span>C</span>
              <p class="kicker">Controller</p>
              <h3>Express handlers</h3>
              <p>Route handlers receive requests, prepare view data and choose the response rendered with <code>res.render()</code>.</p>
            </article>
          </div>

          <div class="mvc-flow" aria-label="MVC request flow">
            <code>Browser request</code><span>→</span><code>Express controller</code><span>→</span><code>Model data</code><span>→</span><code>Handlebars view</code><span>→</span><code>HTML response</code>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="section route-map">
          <div class="section-heading">
            <p class="kicker">Routing map</p>
            <h2>One app, multiple destinations.</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="route-table" role="table" aria-label="Application routes">
            <div class="route-row route-head" role="row"><span>Method</span><span>Path</span><span>Result</span></div>
            <div class="route-row" role="row"><span class="method">GET</span><code>/</code><span>Home view</span></div>
            <div class="route-row" role="row"><span class="method">GET</span><code>/generic</code><span>Fundamentals view</span></div>
            <div class="route-row" role="row"><span class="method">GET</span><code>/elements</code><span>Toolkit view</span></div>
            <div class="route-row" role="row"><span class="method">GET</span><code>/{*splat}</code><span>404 view</span></div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="next-link">
          <p>Continue the tour</p>
          <a href="/elements">Explore the developer toolkit <span>→</span></a>
        </section>
      </main>

      {{> footer}}
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
